IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er4-nouns`
IMPORT `er4-part3-reg63-weekly-indemnity-plan`
IMPORT `er4-part3-regs64-66-other-plans`

-- Tests of regs 64, 65 and 66 (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1074-1108). Every expected value is written by hand from the text.

§ `Fixtures`

-- A section 63 case that meets paragraphs (a), (b), (c), (d) and (g) of reg 63 but FAILS (e) and (f) on purpose:
-- regs 64(b) and 65(a) take over 63 "except the requirements of paragraphs 63(e) and (f)", so it must still pass them.
-- Ruler: hour-bank, commenced, eligible, day-400-hours, elim?, elim days, elim begins at first day, c(i), c(ii), weekly benefit, normal earnings, recurrence, new illness, weeks, events, conditions
`er4 test case 63 failing only (e) and (f)` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, TRUE, 7, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 550, 1000, 99, 99, 1, (LIST `er4 any other event`), EMPTY

GIVEN benefit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test case 63 with weekly benefit` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF FALSE, YearMonthDay 2026 1 15, YearMonthDay 2026 5 1, YearMonthDay 2026 3 20, TRUE, 7, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, benefit, 1000, 99, 99, 1, (LIST `er4 any other event`), EMPTY

`er4 test events of 64(d)` MEANS LIST `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid`
                                   , `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury`
                                   , `er4 the date the insured person retires`
                                   , `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury`

`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)` MEANS LIST `er4 the end of a period during which the benefits are paid`
                                              , `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury`
                                              , `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave`
                                              , `er4 the date the insured person retires`
                                              , `er4 the date of the insured person's separation from employment for a reason other than illness or injury, notice having been given before the onset of the illness or the occurrence of the injury`

-- Ruler: section 63 case, employer, months to reinstate, weeks, events
GIVEN employer IS A `er4 Employer that provides or finances a plan`
      months IS A NUMBER
      weeks IS A NUMBER
      events IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan`
`er4 test special case` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF `er4 test case 63 failing only (e) and (f)`, employer, months, weeks, events

-- Ruler: section 63 case, credits only after the 63(a) period, days credited, days reserved, months deferred, accumulates at the rate, maximum days accumulated, working days of benefit, events
GIVEN after63a IS A BOOLEAN
      credited IS A NUMBER
      reserved IS A NUMBER
      deferred IS A NUMBER
      accumulates IS A BOOLEAN
      maxdays IS A NUMBER
      workdays IS A NUMBER
      events IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
`er4 test cumulative case` MEANS
    `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` OF `er4 test case 63 failing only (e) and (f)`, after63a, credited, reserved, deferred, accumulates, maxdays, workdays, events

-- Ruler: section 65 case, credits only after the 63(a) period, days credited, days reserved, accumulates at the rate, maximum days accumulated, working days of benefit, events
GIVEN five65 IS A `er4 Case under a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
      after63a IS A BOOLEAN
      credited IS A NUMBER
      reserved IS A NUMBER
      accumulates IS A BOOLEAN
      maxdays IS A NUMBER
      workdays IS A NUMBER
      events IS A LIST OF `er4 Event that ends payment of benefits under a plan`
GIVETH A `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan`
`er4 test enhanced case` MEANS
    `er4 Case under an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` OF five65, after63a, credited, reserved, accumulates, maxdays, workdays, events

-- A section 65 case whose (b), (e) and (f) fields FAIL on purpose: 66(a) takes over 65 "except 65(b), 65(c)(i), 65(e) and (f)".
`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)` MEANS
    `er4 test cumulative case` FALSE 0 0 0 FALSE 1 1 (LIST `er4 any other event`)

§ `Reg 64(a) -- who provides or finances the plan`

#ASSERT `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` (`er4 test special case` `er4 Her Majesty in right of a province` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a provincial Crown corporation` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a municipal authority` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a public authority of a province` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` (`er4 test special case` `er4 an institution primarily controlled, supported or financed by a province` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64(a) the plan is provided or financed, in whole or in part, by an employer the paragraph names` (`er4 test special case` `er4 any other employer` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))

§ `Reg 64(b) -- everything in reg 63 except (e) and (f)`

-- The 63 case fails (e) and (f), yet 64(b) is met: those two paragraphs are not required.
#ASSERT `reg 64(b) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a municipal authority` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 63 the plan meets the requirements of a Weekly Indemnity Plan` `er4 test case 63 failing only (e) and (f)`
-- Still required: 63(d), 55% of normal weekly insurable earnings.
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64(b) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` (`er4 Case under a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` OF (`er4 test case 63 with weekly benefit` 549), `er4 a municipal authority`, 1, 52, `er4 test events of 64(d)`)

§ `Reg 64(c) and (d) -- reinstatement after one month; benefits for at least 52 weeks`

#ASSERT `reg 64(c) full benefits are reinstated after one month of active employment` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a municipal authority` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64(c) full benefits are reinstated after one month of active employment` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a municipal authority` 2 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT `reg 64(d) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a municipal authority` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64(d) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a municipal authority` 1 51 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64(d) benefits are payable until the earliest of the four events` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a municipal authority` 1 52 (LIST `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave`))
#ASSERT `reg 64(d) an event at which payment under the plan may end` `er4 the end of the period of incapacity due to the illness or injury`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64(d) an event at which payment under the plan may end` `er4 any other event`

§ `Reg 64 -- all the requirements`

#ASSERT `reg 64 the plan meets the requirements of a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a provincial Crown corporation` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64 the plan meets the requirements of a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test special case` `er4 any other employer` 1 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64 the plan meets the requirements of a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a provincial Crown corporation` 2 52 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 64 the plan meets the requirements of a Special Weekly Indemnity Plan` (`er4 test special case` `er4 a provincial Crown corporation` 1 51 (`er4 test events of 64(d)`))

§ `Reg 65(a) and (b) -- reg 63 except (e) and (f); one or more days credited each full month, one reserved`

#ASSERT `reg 65(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 63 except paragraphs 63(e) and (f)` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT `reg 65(b) the plan credits at least one day of paid sick leave each full month, at least one of them reserved` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT `reg 65(b) the plan credits at least one day of paid sick leave each full month, at least one of them reserved` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 2 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(b) the plan credits at least one day of paid sick leave each full month, at least one of them reserved` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 0.9 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(b) the plan credits at least one day of paid sick leave each full month, at least one of them reserved` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 0 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(b) the plan credits at least one day of paid sick leave each full month, at least one of them reserved` (`er4 test cumulative case` FALSE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))

§ `Reg 65(c) -- what the plan may do notwithstanding paragraph (b)`

-- (i) A credit of 1.5 days a full month, 10 of 20 days actively employed: 0.75 days.
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(i) the paid sick leave credit for a month, prorated in relation to the active employment in the month` 1.5 10 20 EQUALS JUST 0.75
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(i) the paid sick leave credit for a month, prorated in relation to the active employment in the month` 1.5 20 20 EQUALS JUST 1.5
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(i) the paid sick leave credit for a month, prorated in relation to the active employment in the month` 1.5 10 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- (ii) A normal work week of 40 hours: less than twice that (80) in the month may be precluded; 80 itself may not.
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(ii) the plan may preclude the accumulation of paid sick leave for the month` 79 40
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(c)(ii) the plan may preclude the accumulation of paid sick leave for the month` 80 40
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(c)(ii) the plan may preclude the accumulation of paid sick leave for the month` 120 40
-- (iii) The five purposes the paragraph names; anything else it does not mention.
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(iii) the plan may allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home for` `er4 pregnancy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(iii) the plan may allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home for` `er4 caring for a child or children referred to in subsection 23(1) of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(iii) the plan may allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home for` `er4 providing care or support to a family member referred to in subsection 23.1(2) of the Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(iii) the plan may allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home for` `er4 providing care or support to a critically ill child` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(iii) the plan may allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home for` `er4 providing care or support to a critically ill adult` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `reg 65(c)(iii) the plan may allow the insured person to use paid sick leave while remaining at home for` `er4 another purpose` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Reg 65(d), (e) and (f) -- deferral, accumulation, duration`

#ASSERT `reg 65(d) any deferral of eligibility to use paid sick leave is for no more than 12 months` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 12 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT `reg 65(d) any deferral of eligibility to use paid sick leave is for no more than 12 months` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(d) any deferral of eligibility to use paid sick leave is for no more than 12 months` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 13 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT `reg 65(e) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 75 working days` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(e) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 75 working days` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 74 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(e) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 75 working days` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 FALSE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT `reg 65(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 74 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65(f) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 75 (LIST `er4 any other event`))
-- Exhaustion of accumulated sick leave IS one of 65(f)'s five events.
#ASSERT `reg 65(f) an event at which payment under the plan may end` `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave`

§ `Reg 65 -- all the requirements`

#ASSERT `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 12 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 13 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 0 0 TRUE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 FALSE 75 75 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (`er4 test cumulative case` TRUE 1 1 0 TRUE 75 74 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))

§ `Reg 66(a) -- reg 65 except 65(b), (c)(i), (e) and (f)`

-- The embedded 65 case fails 65(b), (e) and (f) on purpose and 66(a) is still met.
#ASSERT `reg 66(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 65 except paragraph 65(b), subparagraph 65(c)(i) and paragraphs 65(e) and (f)` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 65 the plan meets the requirements of a Cumulative Paid Sick Leave Plan` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`)
-- Still required through 66(a): 65(d) (deferral for no more than 12 months).
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(a) the plan satisfies all the requirements of section 65 except paragraph 65(b), subparagraph 65(c)(i) and paragraphs 65(e) and (f)` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case` FALSE 0 0 13 FALSE 1 1 (LIST `er4 any other event`)) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))

§ `Reg 66(b) to (e) -- one and two thirds days; accumulation to 125 working days; benefits for 125 working days`

-- One and two thirds is 5/3: exactly 5/3 meets "one and two thirds or more", 1.66 does not, 2 does.
#ASSERT `reg 66(b) the plan credits at least one and two thirds days of paid sick leave each full month, that many reserved` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE (5 DIVIDED BY 3) (5 DIVIDED BY 3) TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT `reg 66(b) the plan credits at least one and two thirds days of paid sick leave each full month, that many reserved` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(b) the plan credits at least one and two thirds days of paid sick leave each full month, that many reserved` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 1.66 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(b) the plan credits at least one and two thirds days of paid sick leave each full month, that many reserved` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 1.66 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(b) the plan credits at least one and two thirds days of paid sick leave each full month, that many reserved` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) FALSE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
-- 66(c): prorating.
#ASSERT `reg 66(c) the paid sick leave credit for a month, prorated in relation to the active employment in the month` 2 5 20 EQUALS JUST 0.5
#ASSERT `reg 66(c) the paid sick leave credit for a month, prorated in relation to the active employment in the month` 2 5 0 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `reg 66(d) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 125 working days` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(d) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 125 working days` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 124 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(d) unused days accumulate at the prescribed rate up to at least 125 working days` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 FALSE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT `reg 66(e) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(e) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 124 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(e) benefits are payable until the earliest of the five events` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (LIST `er4 any other event`))
#ASSERT `reg 66(e) an event at which payment under the plan may end` `er4 the exhaustion of all accumulated paid sick leave`
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66(e) an event at which payment under the plan may end` `er4 any other event`

§ `Reg 66 -- all the requirements`

#ASSERT `reg 66 the plan meets the requirements of an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave plan` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66 the plan meets the requirements of an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave plan` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 1.5 2 TRUE 125 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
#ASSERT NOT `reg 66 the plan meets the requirements of an Enhanced Cumulative Paid Sick Leave plan` (`er4 test enhanced case` (`er4 test cumulative case failing only (b), (e) and (f)`) TRUE 2 2 TRUE 100 125 (`er4 test events of 65(f) and 66(e)`))
